OL,3,GNEWSACivil War sieges dragged ordinary
OL,4,Afolk into war, says curator
OL,5,
OL,6,F"Sieges were not only the most common
OL,7,Fform of war during the English Civil
OL,8,FWars, but quite often the most brutal,"
OL,9,Fsaid curator Stuart Orme.
OL,11,FThis type of warfare will be explored
OL,12,Fin an exhibition at the Cromwell Museum
OL,13,Fin Huntingdon, which looks beyond
OL,14,Ffamous 17th Century battles such as
OL,15,FEdgehill or Naseby.
OL,17,FBetween 1642 and 1648, the First and
OL,18,FSecond Civil Wars saw 28 major battles
OL,19,Fin England and 189 places were
OL,20,Fbesieged.
